{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## ROOT CAUSE PROVEN — run 30867072561. The instrumentation did exactly what it was built for.\n\nChange 1319's `assert_bridge_alert_for_mutation` took the pass's `CompletedProcess` as a REQUIRED argument and asserted `returncode == 0` BEFORE reading the alert store. That guard is what produced the answer:\n\n    AssertionError: the pass exited 1, not 0 — a failed pass's alert store proves nothing\n    about whether a MUTATION was swallowed, only that the pass itself did not complete.\n\n    stderr: reconcile_once raised: HTTP Error 400\n      url: http://localhost:2990/jira/rest/api/2/issue\n      text: Field 'ticket_type' cannot be set. It is not on the appropriate screen, or unknown.,\n            Field 'title' cannot be set. It is not on the appropriate screen, or unknown.,\n            Field 'status' cannot be set. It is not on the appropriate screen, or unknown.\n\n### THE DEFECT, NAMED\n\nThe outbound CREATE posts rebar's **LOCAL field names** — `ticket_type`, `title`, `status` — to `POST /rest/api/2/issue` as if they were Jira field ids. Jira's are `issuetype` and `summary`, and `status` is not settable at create at all (it is a workflow transition). DC rejects the whole request with 400, so no issue is created, so the binding is never written, so `get_jira_key` returns `None`.\n\n**This is the STRONGER of the two outcomes comment 1 predicted.** No alert was the possibility that would move the bug 'from stage 3 back to stage 1/2' — and that is what happened, one stage further back than even that: the create is not merely unbound, the **entire pass aborts**. `get_jira_key returned None` was a symptom three steps downstream of the actual fault.\n\n**It is NOT the pinned-template change (3fe5).** `ticket_type` and `title` are not Jira fields under ANY template or screen configuration — the error is 'or unknown', and they are unknown. Screen configuration cannot explain a field that does not exist. The same cell failed identically at baseline (run 30857265932), before the template was pinned; only the diagnosis improved.\n\n### AC status\n\n- [x] the failing STAGE is identified — **dispatch**, not bind: `reconcile_once` raises before any issue exists\n- [x] the root cause is proven, not inferred — the 400 names all three offending fields verbatim\n- [ ] the fix makes the cell GREEN on a live harness\n- [ ] an outbound create that fails to bind surfaces an operator-visible signal rather than a pass\n\nThe last AC deserves emphasis given what was just learned: `reconcile_once` raising made the PASS exit 1, which is loud. But the cell that existed before 1319 read only `get_jira_key` and reported a missing binding — so a whole-pass abort was being read as a quiet binding failure. The instrumentation is the operator-visible signal this AC asks for, and it is already merged."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785808202879361001,"uuid":"06527cb3-d0f8-4a0a-895c-bb84dc556b42"}